id: pm-oq893h
title: "POSIX recovery commands are not paste-safe in interactive bash or zsh: a ! inside the double-quoted form triggers history expansion"
description: "Found 2026-11-24 while implementing the shell dialects for pm-kjoudp and GH-1774. The posix renderer in src/core/shared/command-line.ts escapes double quote, backslash, dollar and backtick inside double quotes, which is complete for sh -c and for scripts. An interactive bash with histexpand on (the default) or zsh still expands an exclamation mark inside double quotes: a pasted retry such as pm create --title \"Fix crash!now\" fails with event not found, or substitutes an earlier command. Single quotes suppress history expansion in both shells. Duplicate check: searched history expansion, exclamation, interactive bash, recovery quoting; pm-kjoudp and pm-gh1774 cover cmd.exe and PowerShell only."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 3
tags[3]: agent-ux,posix,recovery
created_at: "2026-11-24T10:36:48.721Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-24T16:18:47.397Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-24T16:18:46.268Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-24T16:18:46.268Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 60
acceptance_criteria: "An argument containing an exclamation mark renders in a form interactive bash and zsh never history-expand, and the URL-credential span spellings register that form; The rendered-command shell-safety integration corpus runs that argument through an interactive bash with histexpand on"
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: low
confidence: high
resolution: "quotePosixCommandArg single-quotes an argument holding ! (with ' escaped as '\\''), so interactive bash and zsh cannot history-expand it. The bare-token rule quotes a token that starts with =, which zsh expands to a command path. The credential registry adds the POSIX single-quote spelling."
expected_result: A pasted POSIX recovery command with ! in an argument runs unchanged in interactive bash and zsh
actual_result: "The shell corpus passes byte for byte through bash with set -o history -o histexpand and through zsh -f, including literal !!, !$ and =node arguments"
